        "suggestion": {
          "candidateIndex": 0,
          "score": 0.57,
          "modelBindingNature": "binding_requirement",
          "sourceQuotation": "As soon as possible after a missed payment has occurred the firm must: (a) notify the borrower: (i) that the missed payment has occurred; and (ii) about any sums which have become payable under the regulated deferred payment credit agreement but remain unpaid (including unpaid charges for non-compliance with the agreement)",
          "citation": "PDF p.95 · legal instrument (FCA 2026/2, Annex F, CONC 7.20.1R(2)(a))",
          "applicabilityConditions": "Applies where a borrower has failed to make a payment by the time it has fallen due under the terms of a regulated deferred payment credit agreement (a 'missed payment'), per CONC 7.20.1R(1). 'Payment' refers to repayment of capital and excludes payment of a charge for non-compliance with the agreement (CONC 7.20.1R(4)). Timing ('as soon as possible') requires firm judgement. The instrument is made (FCA 2026/2); commencement date derived from the supplied provisionLegal evidence (clause H). Draft recommendation requiring human review."
        },
