        "suggestion": {
          "candidateIndex": 1,
          "score": 0.52,
          "modelBindingNature": "binding_requirement",
          "sourceQuotation": "(b) provide the borrower with sufficient information for the borrower to understand: (i) which regulated deferred payment credit agreement the missed payment relates to; (ii) any adverse consequences for the borrower arising out of the missed payment; (iii) any adverse consequences for the borrower that the firm considers are likely to arise out of the missed payment; and (iv) (where relevant) any steps the borrower can take to mitigate those adverse consequences.",
          "citation": "PDF p.95 · legal instrument (FCA 2026/2, Annex F, CONC 7.20.1R(2)(b))",
          "applicabilityConditions": "Applies where there is a missed payment under a regulated deferred payment credit agreement (CONC 7.20.1R(1)); 'payment' means repayment of capital, excluding charges for non-compliance (CONC 7.20.1R(4)). Step (iv) applies only where relevant. Sufficiency of information, scope of adverse consequences, the firm's view of likely consequences and relevance of mitigation steps involve firm judgement; CONC 7.20.2G (guidance, not binding) indicates firms should consider charges for missed payments and credit reference agency reporting. Draft recommendation requiring human review."
        },
